    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1213">

                <pb facs="0857" n="741" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg741"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/266.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Miller to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-03T14:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1914, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Official notices have been issued that all custom Charges for taxes, exportation
                    Charges, oil production taxes and similar Charges must be paid in government
                    offices in Mexican £old: that in lieu of Mexican gold American gold will be
                    accepted for such charges at the rate of two for one.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Miller</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
